  "articleBody": "It's a common thought after a storm: 'Can I just dry this drywall out?' But sometimes, drying isn't enough. If your drywall feels soft or crumbly, or if you see it sagging or pulling away from the wall, that's a big sign it probably needs to be replaced. Another key indicator is any visible mold. Even if you don't see it, a persistent musty smell can mean mold is hidden, and in those cases, replacement is usually the best bet. Plus, if the drywall just isn't drying to normal moisture levels, it’s probably too far gone. Don't forget to consider where the water came from—if it was contaminated, replacement is almost always necessary to protect your home's health. When in doubt, especially with significant damage or suspected mold, it's really smart to get a professional to assess the situation. They can spot hidden issues and ensure a safe, lasting repair. Give HH Remodeling LLC a call for expert storm damage assessment and repair in the greater Denver area.",
